  "merger_description": "Covetrus, Inc. (**Covetrus**) proposes to acquire 100% of the shares in MWI Veterinary Supply, Inc. (**MWI Animal Health**).\n\nCovetrus\u00a0is a global wholesale distributor of animal health products, including pharmaceuticals, nutrition, medical devices and consumables. Covetrus also supplies veterinary practice management software, including Covetrus Ascend, RxWorks, Vetlytics, VisionVPM. Covetrus is currently jointly controlled by funds managed and/or advised by TPG Inc. (**TPG**) and funds managed and/or advised by\u00a0Clayton, Dubilier & Rice, LLC (**CD&R**).\n\nTPG\u00a0is a global alternative asset manager firm. TPG has interests in\u00a0Greencross Vets, an Australian provider of\u00a0veterinary services, pet services and pet retail stores (through its Petbarn and City Farmers brands).\u00a0CD&R is a private equity investment group based in the United States.\n\nMWI Animal Health is currently a subsidiary of Cencora Inc. MWI Animal Health is a multinational wholesale distributor of animal health products, including pharmaceuticals, nutrition and veterinary instruments. MWI Animal Health also supplies a veterinary practice management software called Merlin.",
